<description>
Rotate each magenta source pixel 90 degrees counterclockwise around its matched blue pivot, recoloring the new pixel orange.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- The only foreground colors are blue pivot pixels and magenta source pixels.
- Each magenta source can be paired one-to-one with a blue pivot in the same
  row or column.

Rule:
- Remove all magenta source pixels.
- For each matched source/pivot pair, preserve the source distance from the
  pivot but rotate its offset 90 degrees counterclockwise.
- Paint the rotated in-bounds target orange; if the target is outside the
  grid, the source simply disappears.

Key insight:
The blue pixels are rotation centers, and row/column alignment gives a
unique global matching from each magenta source to its pivot.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "magenta source pixel s",
  "dst": "blue pivot pixel d",
  "match_cond": "s and d are uniquely aligned in the same row or same column",
  "transform": "clear s; rotate s.offset around d 90 degrees counterclockwise; paint in-bounds target orange"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: N x N square, N in 8-16 [observed]
  background: azure (8)
  colors: exactly {background, blue (1), magenta (6)} in input; output replaces magenta with orange (7)
  pixels:
    blue_pivots: 3-7 single blue pixels scattered on background
    magenta_sources: same count as blue pivots; each shares exactly one row or column with a blue pivot
  matching: one-to-one pairing of sources to pivots via shared row/col; must be globally unique (no ambiguous alternate matching)
  source_pivot_distance: Manhattan 1-4 per pair; mix of same-row (~30%) and same-col (~70%) alignments [observed]
  transformation:
    remove all magenta; for each (source, pivot) pair rotate source 90 degrees CCW around pivot
    CCW rotation of offset (dr, dc) becomes (-dc, dr); paint in-bounds target orange
    if rotated target is out of grid bounds, source simply disappears (0-2 OOB per puzzle)
  constraints:
    - all rotated in-bounds targets must land on background (no collisions with blue or other targets)
    - source directions relative to pivot vary (above/below/left/right all occur)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick N from 8-16; create N x N azure grid
    2. pick K pairs from 3-7; place K blue pivot pixels at random positions (no two sharing both row and col)
    3. for each pivot, choose a random CCW-rotation offset (dr, dc) with Manhattan distance 1-4
       compute source = (pivot_r + dr, pivot_c + dc), target = (pivot_r - dc, pivot_c + dr)
       source must be in-bounds, on background, and share row or col with its pivot (guaranteed by axis-aligned offset)
       target either OOB (allowed) or in-bounds on background; allow 0-2 OOB total
    4. verify the global source-pivot matching is unique (backtrack-search); retry if ambiguous
    5. output grid = input with magenta removed and in-bounds targets painted orange
    6. input grid = blue pivots + magenta sources on azure background
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

